The neighbourhood:
Among the best neighbourhoods of Lisbon, with large houses, palaces and carefully preserved mansions, this is a quiet and important area. Lapa itself is known as the embassy district. It is one of the most pleasant districts of Lisbon, with large and old houses perfectly preserved, many of them old palaces and palaces. The imposing Basilica da Estrela marks the meeting point of many groups, just in front of Jardim da Estrela, where the elders spend the afternoon playing cards and the children have fun in the playground. This garden at the top is the only flat spot, and the whole neighbourhood unfolds down one of the several hills of Lisbon. Thus, as in other parts of the city, many of the houses have breath taking views over the city. One can see the Tagus River and the 25 de Abril Bridge in the distance.

The centre of political life in Portugal is in São Bento, in the Assembly of the Republic. From here comes the name of this neighbourhood, which unfolds around a street, the street of S. Bento, which runs from the Palace of S. Bento to Largo do Rato. It is an important link between Santos, Estrela and the Amoreiras. Here live the new generations of families with roots in Lisbon. With a number of parks around it, including the Jardim das Flores, the area in front of the Assembly and the Jardim da Estrela, this is a good place for recent and growing families 
